Debug lines only: GNOME Settings 46.7 sound panel decisions that log nothing.

Not for upstream submission. Adds g_debug() under the panel's existing log
domain (cc-sound-panel, set in panels/meson.build), printed only when
G_MESSAGES_DEBUG names that domain. No behaviour change.

  * output/input_device_update_cb: which device the combo box returned when
    gvc's active-*-update arrived, how many profiles the Configuration combo
    then held, whether the row was shown or hidden, and whether the volume
    slider / level meter stream was replaced or kept (U4, the "Configuration
    line disappears" mark, U6).
  * output/input_device_changed_cb: the device and stream picked when the
    combo box changes (also fires on programmatic changes from gvc).
  * cc_profile_combo_box_set_device: the early return that keeps the profile
    list when the device object is unchanged, and the rebuilt list (U1, U4).
  * profile_changed_cb: the profile the user picked (U1).

Applies to the upstream tag 46.7 (checked with patch --dry-run -p1). Ubuntu's
1:46.7-0ubuntu0.24.04.6 carries two feature patches in panels/sound; check
with patch --dry-run against the Ubuntu source before building.

